# subsystems: screen (src/screen), window (src/app.rs, src/session), scripts (zyt-script, src/scripts.rs), source (zyt-serial, zyt-pty)
# Now: the code as it is.
title The screen: to_screen, the cache of the state and the page of the window
lanes Source | Screen | Channels | Script | Window

node drv outside 0 | Port or pty | Thread of the source: driver, rx, tx.
node rx buffer 0 | rx | The read buffer of the source, with a limit: full, the port is not read.
node tx buffer 0 | tx | The write queue of the source.
node screen group 1 | Thread of the screen | One per window; waits on Wake, IDLE 250 ms.
node term terminal 1 in=screen | Terminal | Its one owner; feed.
node cache buffer 1 in=screen | Said::state | On the Board: TermState (modes, character sets, cursor shape, title) and the bytes of the echo fed.
node board buffer 1 in=screen | Board | The page and Said, under a short lock.
node ts buffer 2 | to_screen | ByteSwap of the run; a write waits while 64 KiB wait (ScreenCommand::Echo).
node script code 3 | Thread of the script | Lua: zyt.line.read and write, zyt.term.write, zyt.notice.
node client outside 3 | Telnet client | A socket.
node win code 4 | Window | App::logic, Session::pump, take_screen; App::ui draws.

view Now / script | The echo and the notices go to the screen through to_screen; no frame on the way.
edge drv > rx | read
edge rx > script | zyt.line.read | as much as it needs; rx full, the port waits
edge script > client | client:write
edge script > tx | zyt.line.write
edge tx > drv | write
edge script > ts | zyt.term.write, zyt.notice | after the client; waits in slices while full
edge ts > term | print, follow off
edge term > cache | TermState, when the turn fed the terminal
edge cache ~> script | zyt.term.state | state_reader, in the thread of the script
edge term > board | snapshot.take, put
edge board > win | take: swap of the page
show screen

view Now / script / turn | One Screen::turn while a script owns the line. The window takes no part until the turn ends.
phase Turn of the screen | Rung by a write into to_screen, by the window; else IDLE.
step screen > screen | take_commands | Resize, Line, Input, Print
step screen > screen | no read of rx | the script owns the line; answers of the terminal are dropped
step ts > term | take_echo | fed to the plain terminal
step screen > screen | take_events | title, bell, clipboard
step term > cache | update the cache | put with each publish
step term > board | publish | the page and Said, when something changed
step board ~> win | shown() | request_repaint
phase Frame of the window | When eframe gives one; a hidden window seldom or never.
step win > board | take_screen | swap of the page, copy of Said
step win > win | ui | draws the page

view Now / no script | No script: the screen is the one reader of rx; the window draws and sends commands.
edge drv > rx | read
edge rx > term | read_into, feed | the screen
edge term > tx | answer | answers of the terminal
edge win > tx | ScreenCommand::Input | keys; the screen writes them through its Lease
edge tx > drv | write
edge term > cache | TermState, when the turn fed the terminal
edge term > board | snapshot.take, put
edge board > win | take: swap of the page
show screen

view Now / no script / turn | One Screen::turn with no script. The window takes no part until the turn ends.
phase Turn of the screen | Rung by the source, by the window; else IDLE.
step win > screen | commands | Input, Resize, Print: take_commands
step screen > tx | Input | keys into tx
step rx > term | read | read_into, feed; held while a selection is made
step term > tx | answer | answers of the terminal
step screen > screen | take_events | title, bell, clipboard
step term > cache | update the cache | put with each publish
step term > board | publish | the page and Said, when something changed
step board ~> win | shown() | request_repaint
phase Frame of the window | When eframe gives one; a hidden window seldom or never.
step win > board | take_screen | swap of the page, copy of Said
step win > win | ui | draws the page

note Subsystems: screen, window, scripts, source.
note The window gets what it draws only as the page on the Board, in its own frame. The cache of the state is for a script; the window does not read it.
note While the window draws nothing, the screen and the script go on: the Board keeps the last page.
note The counters of the line are read by the window from the source (line.scheme), not from Said.
